      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ilioupoli enjoys a sunny climate that fuels annual festivals and hiking trails along the nearby Hymettus mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ilioupoli",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town promotes sustainable urban living while preserving its historic character, making it a quieter alternative to central Athens.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ilioupoli",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ilioupoli is part of the Attica region, which covers about 3,808 square kilometres and includes the Athens metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attica_(region)",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Attica region, which includes Ilioupoli, is coextensive with the former Attica Prefecture of Central Greece.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
